  "faithful": "Telcaceous animals are not only extremely different in external form, but also in the mode of their production. Some are viviparous, as the mot of tho which inhabit bivalve shells, multivalves, and even fome of the univalves; while the others, which form the far greater proportion, are oviparous. In one point, however, they all agree, that whatever be the mode of production, whether from an egg, or directly from the uterus of the mother, the shell is formed on the body of the young animal, and is proportioned to its bulk.",
  "modern": "Telcaceous animals are not only extremely different in external form, but also in the mode of their production. Some are viviparous, as the mot of tho which inhabit bivalve shells, multivalves, and even some of the univalves; while the others, which form the far greater proportion, are oviparous. In one point, however, they all agree, that whatever be the mode of production, whether from an egg, or directly from the uterus of the mother, the shell is formed on the body of the young animal, and is proportioned to its bulk."
